  "body": "The specification for [canvas filters](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#filters) is not clear about how `url()` references to filters declared in inline SVGs in the DOM should work in the context of Shadow DOM.\r\n\r\nProposal: resolve local hash URLs relative to where the canvas element is located in the (shadow)DOM so that a filter can be referenced if the canvas that created the canvas context is located in the same shadow DOM as the inline SVG that declares the filter. \r\nIf the canvas is not connected to the DOM, resolve the relative URL against the document root - or whatever the current spec says in the absence of shadow doms.\r\n\r\nI created this issue as per suggestion in [this comment](https://github.com/w3c/webcomponents/issues/179#issuecomment-477670644).",
